{
  "title": "SKY130 NFET f_T vs width",
  "group": "SKY130 transistors",
  "description": "SKY130 NFET f_T vs width (fixture-free AC parameter sweep)",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 170,
        "y": -118,
        "title": "SKY130 NFET f_T vs width — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "A single NFET MN1 is biased at Vgs = 1.2 V (VG1) and",
          "Vds = 1.8 V (VD1), source grounded. The AC sweep",
          "(10 MHz -> 1 THz) gives current gain h21; f_T is where",
          "|h21| = 1. Here MN1.w_um is swept 0.5 -> 8 um.",
          "f_T ~ gm / (2*pi*Cgg): gm and Cgg both scale with width,",
          "so f_T stays nearly flat as the device gets wider.",
          "",
          "Set MN1.l_um = 0.5 and re-run to see f_T drop at every",
          "width -- f_T falls steeply with channel length."
        ]
      }
    ],
